.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "" "Simple Shell" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
simple_shell - a simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./simple_shell

.SH DESCRIPTION
simple_shell reads one command per line and executes it using fork and execve.
.PP
Only a full path (absolute or relative) to an executable is supported;
the shell does not search PATH yet.
.PP
Each command line must be a single word; arguments are not supported.
.PP
No special characters are handled: " ' ` \\ * & #
.PP
If the executable is not found, an error message is printed and the
prompt is shown again.
.PP
It works in interactive and non-interactive mode.

.SH USAGE
Run the shell with:

.nf
$ ./simple_shell
.fi

.SH BUILTIN COMMANDS
No built-in commands are implemented at this stage.

.SH EOF
Ctrl-D (EOF) exits the shell cleanly.

